Description: autotests: Let the DMA-BUF format switch test run with assertions
 With a debug KWayland the test aborted on its second frame: Surface::commit()
 asks for a frame callback by default, and the next commit asked for another
 before the first one had come back (ASSERT "!frameCallbackInstalled" in
 KWayland's surface.cpp). The test waits for KWin's own frameRendered, so
 it commits without a frame callback, as the other integration tests do.
 .
 Its buffers were GraphicsBuffers deleted through std::unique_ptr, which
 GraphicsBuffer's destructor refuses (ASSERT "m_dropped"); they are dropped
 now.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Origin: https://invent.kde.org/danielcamposramos/kwin/-/commit/26981f2b17a5e1fcdd374eb0888e2eecaaa0a076
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-22
Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
